 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>64\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 69\u00b0F, and the record is 81\u00b0F (2021). The low of <strong>49\u00b0F</strong> was the 4th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 94 since 1932.","t_rec":"Palmdale has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Palmdale's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Palmdale has set <strong class=\"sig\">19 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 104 that chance alone would give, and <strong>144 record highs</strong>, more than the 104 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (68). Palmdale's all-time high is 118\u00b0F, on August 5, 1990.","t_chg":"Palmdale has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 91 complete years: Palmdale's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.48\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.36 to +0.61), about +4.5\u00b0F since 1933. Palmdale's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.26\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.36), about +2.4\u00b0F since 1933.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Palmdale's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.29 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 6.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1943 (18.98 in); the driest, 1953 (0.86 in). Palmdale almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 12 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}